# Docs/Spec/Reference/cli.md: `jet check Core` reports Core's own lints, and a program that
# only uses Core reports none of them. The probe program calls `log.bool`, whose Core signature
# carries a lint (a public function's positional `Bool`), so the program's check reaches Core code
# that holds a lint and drops it. The tree adds a float equality (L0502) to core.log that only the
# every-body check reaches, so `jet check Core` has a lint of its own to print. That check also
# demands the codec bodies the compiler generates for Core types (core.db's DBError codec): a lint
# there names Core source, never the check's scratch entry. Core's lints print as warnings, so
# the check still ends with no errors.
env: NO_COLOR=1
requires: os:unix
fixture: CheckCoreLints.fixture
copy: {root}/Core tree/Core
copy: {root}/Compiler/Prelude tree/Compiler/Prelude
concat: tree/Core/Log/Log.jet tree/Core/Log/Log.jet lint.txt
step: jet check tree/app/probe.jet
env: JET_TOOLCHAIN_ROOT={work}/tree
exit: 0
stdout+stderr: ~ "has no problems" # the program reports none of Core's lints
stdout+stderr: !~ "Warning" # not even the ones on the Core code its call reaches
step: jet check tree/Core
unset: JET_TOOLCHAIN_ROOT
exit: 0
stdout+stderr: ~ "has no errors" # Core's lints are warnings
stdout+stderr: ~ "Comparing floats" # Core's own lint
stdout+stderr: !~ "jet-check-core" # no lint against the check's scratch entry
